<http://fdp.dcc.sib.swiss/catalog/64136f6d-1e2b-557d-8c9d-5704e7c4c2e9> a dcat:Catalog,
        dcat:Resource ;
    rdfs:label "Personalized, Data-driven Prediction and Assessment of Infection Related Outcomes in Swiss ICUs (IICU)" ;
    ns5:applicableLegislation <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2013/617/de>,
        <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2013/642/de>,
        <https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2022/491/de>,
        "Cantonal data protection laws" ;
    ns3:minTypicalAge 18 ;
    ns3:numberOfUniqueIndividuals 67442 ;
    dcterms:abstract "Infections show diverse endotypes and phenotypes that influence clinical outcomes. The Personalized Swiss Sepsis Study (PSSS) and clinical data warehouses have improved integration of host, pathogen, and longitudinal data, but key gaps remain: limited clinical context and insufficient interpretation of clinical phenotypes. Understanding which interventions occurred and why is essential for patient management. We will develop harmonized clinical annotation for infections, outcomes, and contextual interpretation to support expert-informed and data-driven assessment on ICUs. Our goals are to maintain and expand the PSSS platform beyond sepsis under FAIR principles, improve data quality through standardized phenotype and context annotation, build a sustainable network across ICUs, infectious diseases, microbiology, and data science, develop clinical and computational methods for rapid and precise patient assessmentâincluding multidimensional characterization, early outcome prediction, digital biomarker validation, and treatment evaluationâand create a multicenter FAIR public data repository with software for phenotype assessment, biomarker discovery, and retrospective validation." ;
